    "body": "## What\n\nFix the background bash card regression reported after #12. Running bash cards remain mutable until their terminal result instead of retiring into immutable terminal history when the call backgrounds. Preserve the existing detached-task retirement behavior.\n\nExtend the existing live/rebuilt-card regression with acknowledged terminal-history pressure, remove an obsolete test that required background bash updates to stop, and document compact live cards under viewport pressure.\n\n## Why\n\nThe walkthrough card stopped repainting after roughly 30 seconds even though the job kept producing output. Reproduction showed the card retiring when later conversation exceeded the viewport, not a 30-second job timeout.\n\n## Testing\n\n- The pressure regression failed before the fix (the live viewport was empty) and passes after it.\n- Focused background-output, event-controller, async-task lifecycle, and transcript suites: 59 tests passed, 206 assertions.\n- Actual source BashTool, job manager, ToolExecutionComponent, TranscriptContainer, and production Composer exercised in a real tmux PTY with a sustained ping. At 30 seconds, later conversation exceeded the viewport. Before the fix the card committed while backend output continued; after the fix the card stayed active, its compact row showed 58 seconds, and enlarging the terminal revealed icmp_seq=34 with elapsed 75.32 seconds.\n- The full local check:ts command reached its 180-second deadline. Authoritative exact-head CI #119 and merged-source CI #122 both passed: workspace lint/format/type checks, Rust checks, web/native/CLI builds, and the exact compiled-version assertion.\n- Fork CI test suites remain disabled by existing policy; this PR does not re-enable them. CI retains lint/format/type/Rust checks, web/native/CLI builds, and compiled-version verification.\n- No changelog change: not requested. No local native or shipping build, and no installation.\n\n- Merged into integration as `1c657a066e44b7d7b17a577c421f60f7160ffbc5`; the feature branch is preserved.\n- Arch pipeline #217 succeeded with the exact merged source, recipe `8a6eb2b8b4d1b82d34ac94b26c36e5d46cff8cd2`, and package `oh-my-pi-vith-git`. Published package: `18.4.8.vith.r335.g1c657a066e44-1`.\n- Downloaded the published package and signed repository database. Both signatures verify against trusted key `433D492D0438666BBB7230BB91D0A55E51016A94`; the database filename/version/size/SHA256 match the package. SHA256: `9abc052f4ddffea192cc559cb4da27bb68400a7a6bddcbb7e8aa90bd0efd4c96`.\n- The binary extracted from the published package reports `omp/18.4.8+vith-fork.335.1c657a066e44`. No installation was performed.\n\n---\n\n- [x] `bun check` passes\n- [x] Tested locally\n- [ ] CHANGELOG updated with the required attribution (if user-facing; internal issue fixes use issue links, external contributions add the PR link and contributor credit after creation)",
